# AI capabilities

Owning services publish tools. AI discovers them and applies **generic** completion only.

Related: [ai-project.mdc](ai-project.mdc), [ai-agent skill](../skills/ai-agent/SKILL.md).

## Ownership

| Layer | Owns | Must not |
|-------|------|----------|
| AI (`ai/backend/src/ai/tools`) | `parseTool`, `completeCreateArgs`, `pickHexColor`, executor, generic system prompt | Tool-name switches, palettes, status rules, `create_*` field copy |
| Peer (`<service>/backend/src/ai/capabilities.ts`) | `jsonSchema`, tool `description`, optional `argCompletion` | Putting domain rules in the AI service |

## `argCompletion` (optional, on write tools)

```ts
argCompletion?: {
  allowedKeys?: string[]
  defaults?: Record<string, unknown>
  forceByRole?: Partial<Record<ToolRole, Record<string, unknown>>>
  uniqueBy?: string
  uniqueLookup?: { method: 'GET'; path: string; queryParam: 'names' }
  pascalCaseKeys?: string[]
}
```

AI applies, in order: missing `defaults` → random hex color from schema `enum` or a generic fallback palette (same `Math.random` index as the tag create form) → `forceByRole[role]` → capitalize the first letter of each `pascalCaseKeys` string (PharmacyInventory, not pharmacyInventory) → drop keys not in `allowedKeys`. If `jsonSchema.required` keys are still missing, the executor returns `MISSING_REQUIRED_ARGS` to the model instead of asking the user to confirm.

When parking create writes, AI looks up `uniqueBy` values via `uniqueLookup` (`GET path?names=`). Existing names and in-batch duplicates are skipped; only missing unique values are shown for confirm. Never switch on tool names such as `create_data_tag`.

Keep the type in sync on peer `capabilityTypes.ts` and `ai/backend/src/ai/tools/registry.ts`. `parseTool` must copy `argCompletion` and `relatedArgs` through.

## `relatedArgs` (optional, on write tools)

Applies to **create and update** write tools. When the user attaches entity context and asks to suggest or add missing related items, peers must publish `relatedArgs` on the matching `update_*` tool so the confirm row and nested checkbox tree appear instead of prose-only suggestions.

```ts
relatedArgs?: {
  argKey: string
  displayKey: string
  getPath: string
  listPath: string
  createTool: string
  cardinality?: 'one' | 'many'
  itemIdKey?: string
}[]
```

Confirm UI never shows opaque `*_id` values. AI looks up related records (GET by id or list `?names=`), nests them under the **parent** confirm row as a checkbox tree, and fills every related `jsonSchema` property. Recurse into `createTool.relatedArgs` (depth cap 3). Do not park related creates as sibling confirm rows.

- `exists`: already in the library — checkbox checked and disabled; confirm only links the id.
- new: checkbox checked by default; uncheck to skip create and skip the FK.
- Confirm `POST .../confirm` may send `{ relatedSelections: { [path]: boolean } }`. Unchecked new nodes are omitted. Existing nodes always attach.
- `cardinality: 'many'` plus optional `itemIdKey` maps selected ids onto arrays (`tag_ids` or `attributes: [{ attribute_id }]`).

Never switch on tool names such as `create_data_attribute`.

## `viewPath` (optional, on tools that return records)

Owning service publishes a frontend path template (`/services/{id}`, `/data/{kind}/{id}`). AI interpolates `{id}` / `{kind}` from the record (and tool args) and attaches `__open` for the chat UI. Do not hard-code tool names in AI. Data paths are the Data FE routes; WebOnOne prefixes `/data` when opening them.

## Color

- Peer: publish `#RRGGBB` `enum` on the color property (same list as that service’s UI).
- AI: `pickHexColor(palette)` only — random index from the published enum, matching Data UI `randomTagColor`. No meaning maps (clinic/health), no copied tag palettes.

## Prompts

`DEFAULT_SYSTEM_PROMPT` and `withAvailableToolsPrompt` stay generic. On every create suggestion, fill **all** `jsonSchema.properties` (required and optional), not only `required`. Remainder tables use `suggestCreateKeys` (required first, then the rest). List related records with matching `list_*` tools first; copy `*_id` / `*_ids` from those results — never invent IDs. When the model lists create-ready records, call `create_*` once per item. If the user asks for N items, park N confirm rows. Models often emit one `create_*` call; AI then asks for a markdown table of the remaining items (all schema columns, no tools) and lifts those rows. Existing unique names are skipped. Never ask which items to create in text — the shared Confirm ItemList is the picker (Confirm / Skip per row). Field rules belong on the tool `description`. Do not switch on tool names such as `create_data_tag`.

Peer `create_*` and `update_*` `description` must tell the model to suggest every published property. Related records use names (via `relatedArgs`), not opaque ids, with matching `list_*` tools. Suggest only related records that fit the parent — do not dump the whole library. When entity context is attached and the user asks to fill missing related items, call the matching `update_*` write tool (not prose) so Confirm/Skip UI can park the change.

Reference: `data/backend/src/ai/capabilities.ts` (`create_data_tag`), `ai/backend/src/ai/tools/createDefaults.ts`.

